This marks the completion of my 2 week work placement at UCL ARC. I will be going over what I've done this week and overall my take away from this placement

## Project Completion
We have finished going through the list of open source programs and analysing them. Over this week we have created a program to automatically send out these issues to each repository.
I hope these issues are informative and useful to those of you who have received them!
Next, I will be working on a project report and poster to collate and finalise this project. I will be presenting this research to the Research Stem team celebratory event later on in the year.

## Highlights
- On Tuesday, I presented to the UCL ARC Forum about myself and the project me and Tasmin are carrying out. This was an amazing experience to work on my public speaking skills aswell as making myself known to the staff. It was quite nerve-wracking at first; however over time I adjusted and it was quite a good experience overall.
- On Thursday, I went to Tesco in Holborn for lunch and was amazed by the fact that the self serving machine automatically detected what was in my hand without me having to scan it. This fascinated me as I've never been to a tesco that's done that before and it was interesting thinking about it.
We also worked with David on creating an algorithm to automatically send out issues from our spreadsheet. This was interesting as he taught us various different libraries and explained each step. This allowed me to continue more and develop on my coding skills.
- On Friday, we worked on analysing more repos and sending out the issues with the program we made.

Overall, I'm so thankful I was chosen on this placement. I learned a lot whether that be relating to my project or learning about new fields I never considered before. Hearing about other peoples projects and advice has opened my eyes to how broad computer science as a whole is. I'm very excited for what the future holds for me!
Thank you UCL ARC for these amazing 2 weeks!
